  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The three Tormach lathe files now state `\"rigid_tapping\": true`: `tormach-8l.mch`, `tormach-15l-slant-pro.mch` and `tormach-15lx-slant-pro.mch`.\n- The pin now checks the lathes. Its new name is `every_tormach_mill_router_and_lathe_file_states_rigid_tapping`. It expects exactly three Tormach lathes. The plasma table stays outside the check.\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` now says that the Tormach lathes state the key.\n- `docs/decisions/795-lathe-rigid-tapping.md` cites the manuals.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe lathe files did not state the key. The Machines pane read them as \"not stated - not limited\". The research comment on #795 found the answer in each operator manual:\n\n- 8L: UM10753, section 10.3.18 \"Rigid Tapping (G33.1)\".\n- 15L Slant-PRO: UM10225, section 6.5.17.\n- 15LX Slant-PRO: UM10860, section 10.3.13.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `rigid_tapping::every_tormach_mill_router_and_lathe_file_states_rigid_tapping`.\n- Red before the fix: `assertion left == right failed: Tormach 8L, left: None, right: Some(true)`.\n- Mutations: I removed the key from each lathe file, one at a time. The pin failed each time and named the machine (`Tormach 8L`, `Tormach 15L Slant-PRO`, `Tormach 15LX Slant-PRO`). With the key restored, the pin passes.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): green. It ran `probe_no_coolant` and `rigid_tapping`.\n- I also ran `machine_library`, `machine`, `posting` and `tormach_lathes`. All pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Posted output does not change. The program gate refuses a tap only on a stated `false`. The post script default for `machine.rigidTapping` is already `true`. `tormach-lathe.cps` still refuses a `TAP` cycle by name.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No lathe tap output. G33.1 output in `tormach-lathe.cps` is later work. The decision file lists the rules from the manuals for that work.\n- No check on a real PathPilot lathe control.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nChangelog: The Tormach 8L, 15L Slant-PRO and 15LX Slant-PRO machine files state rigid tapping (true, from their operator manuals); the Machines pane shows \"yes\" for them.\n\nFixes #795\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
